INT. COLLAPSED PARKING GARAGE, LEVEL P3 - NIGHT

Dust hangs in the beam of a headlamp. Concrete slab above, a tilted pillar, an overturned sedan with its radio humming.

A WOMAN hunches in the gap between slab and floor. Fifties, parka, scraped palms. She is wedged tight and breathing carefully.

WOMAN
(to herself)
Slow in. Slow out.

The sedan radio crackles. A voice on a rescue frequency.

RESCUER (V.O.)
Hello? Can anyone hear me? This is Ines Calderon, Urban Rescue Team Four.

The woman lifts her head.

WOMAN
I hear you.

RESCUER (V.O.)
Ma'am, what's your name?

WOMAN
Beatrix. Beatrix Oyelowo-Marsh.

RESCUER (V.O.)
Beatrix, are you hurt?

BEATRIX
Wrist. Maybe rib. I'm stuck, not bleeding.

RESCUER (V.O.)
Good. We're coming. Stay still.

BEATRIX
I'm not going anywhere.

She almost laughs. Dust sifts down onto her shoulders. She lowers her head onto her arm and watches the beam of her headlamp tremble on the concrete.
